Let $\sigma(n)$ denote the sum of all positive divisors of a positive integer $n$. Prove the following:
(1) $\frac{\sigma(n)}{n} \leqslant \log _{2}(2 n)$;
(2) For any given positive integer $k$, there exist infinitely many positive integers $n$ such that $\frac{\sigma(n)}{n} > k$.

